    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll implement the batch reject action based on the existing batch approve functionality. Let me first explore the codebase to understand the current structure.\n\nNow I understand the structure. Let me also check the app package to understand the Identity structure:\n\nNow I have a complete understanding. Let me check if there are any tests I can run:\n\nGood, the project builds. Now I'll implement the batch reject action. Based on the existing approve implementation, I need to:\n\n1. Add the reject handler in `internal/candidate/approval.go`\n2. Register the new route in `protocol.Routes`\n\nLet me implement this:\n\nLet me read the file again to see the current state:\n\nI see the file still has `fingerprint(ids)` without the `op` parameter. I need to fix that and add the reject handler. Let me do this step by step:\n\nNow let me verify the file compiles correctly:\n\nGood. Now let me run tests to verify everything works:\n\nLet me verify the final file to ensure it's correct:\n\nThe implementation is complete. Let me verify one more time with `go vet` and a final build:\n\nImplementation complete. The bulk-reject Action has been added with:\n\n1. **New handler function** `reject` that:\n   - Validates input (zero-byte IDs return 404)\n   - Starts a transaction and sets session context\n   - Acquires advisory lock using operation name, tenant, actor, and key\n   - Checks `ActionRequest` for idempotency (same key → returns replayed result, different hash → 409)\n   - Queries eligible purchases (submitted, other-user, same tenant) with `FOR UPDATE`\n   - Returns 409 if any target is missing/invalid (indistinguishable from existing behavior)\n   - Updates status to `'rejected'`\n   - Inserts `ApprovalAudit` rows with `operation='bulk-reject.v4'` and `toStatus='rejected'`\n   - Inserts/updates `ActionRequest` with `operation='bulk-reject.v4'`\n   - Returns 200 with `{\"rejectedIds\":[sorted IDs]}` and `Idempotency-Replayed` header\n\n2. **Route registration** in `protocol.Routes`: `\"/purchases/bulk-reject\": reject`\n\n3. **Constants**: `opReject = \"bulk-reject.v4\"`\n\n4. **Updated fingerprint function** to accept operation name parameter\n\nThe implementation follows the exact same patterns as the existing `bulk-approve` Action, ensuring consistency with the codebase while meeting all the requirements for batch rejection with proper idempotency, transaction handling, and concurrency control."
